    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 5 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Capture cards from the table by matching rank or by matching the sum of two or more table cards; score points for sweeps (scopa), most cards, most coins/diamonds, the seven of coins (settebello), and the best primiera; first to 11 or more points wins the game.',
      'Turn-flow example: 1. Deal: Each player receives three cards; four cards are dealt face up to the table; remaining cards form the stock.\n2. Play: Non-dealer plays first. On each turn, play one card from hand. If it matches a single table card by value, capture that card; if it equals the sum of two or more table cards, capture that set; otherwise leave the played card on the table. When you capture all table cards (sweep), that is a scopa and scores 1 point.\n3. After each player has played three cards, the dealer gives three more cards to each player (no new table cards). Repeat until all cards are played.\n4. End of hand: Remaining table cards go to the last captor. Score for scope, most cards, most coins, settebello, and best primiera. First to 11+ points wins.',
      'Scoring example: One point per scopa (sweep); one point each for most cards, most coins/diamonds, seven of coins (settebello), and best primiera. First to 11 or more points wins. First player or team to reach 11 or more points after a hand wins the game; if tied, play another hand to break the tie..',
